{
  "_fonte": "EXP grid: exponent of d in the per-token separability (open limit (a) of the token KAT). Pre-registered in the EXP addendum; single source for the analytic table and for the literal token-budget simulation. Never edit after its sha256 is recorded.",
  "_custos": "k in tokens per event: 14 = compact transaction encoding; 55 = plain-text transaction; K = 2048 = context length. Same inputs as the token KAT grid.",
  "_desenho": "Both combos (R and R plus S) saturated. Family C: R has a single source A and S a different cost; the theory improves iff r^2 > kappa (r = d_S/d_A, kappa = k_S/k_A); d_S = d_A * kappa^(1/e) with e = 1.6 (low side) or 2.5 (high side), 3 decimals. Family D: homogeneous cost k = 14, R with a rare strong source and a frequent weak one (rate weights 0.15/0.85, d_B = 0.1 d_A); the theory improves iff d_S > mu_2 (rate-weighted power mean of order 2); d_S = mu_1.6 (low) or mu_2.5 (high), 3 decimals.",
  "_tag": "tag enters the random stream default_rng([seed, i_cell, i_combo, tag, i_block]); 5 is exclusive to this family (3 = token KAT; 6, 7, 8 = the other three families of the same batch).",
